"""One listening library for all retained question intents, preserving old URLs."""
from html import escape as e
import json
from pathlib import Path
from build_question_overview import document,clock,p,table
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];D=ROOT/'research/question-audio-complete'
def player(url,label):return '<audio controls preload="none" aria-label="'+e(label)+'"><source src="'+e(url)+'" type="audio/wav"></audio>'
def main():
 d=json.loads((D/'library.json').read_text());clips=d['clips'];new=json.loads((D/'audio.json').read_text())['clips'];enroll=sum(c['separate_enrollment_after_question'] for c in new);subset=json.loads((D/'evaluation-subset.json').read_text());frozen={q['question_id'] for q in subset['evaluation_questions']}
 body='<header class="hero"><span class="eyebrow">Question audio library</span><h1>Listen to all 105 questions</h1><p class="lede">Each question has a synthesized request beginning “Assistant,” in the requester’s voice, an insertion into a short recording excerpt, and a separate original-voice comparison.</p><p>92 missing question recordings are now added to the existing 13. The library counts distinct questions; alternate phrasings and the original three-model comparisons do not increase this total. Answer generation remains deferred.</p></header>'
 body+='<section class="section" id="method"><h2>How these clips are made</h2><ol><li><strong>Question selection.</strong> Input: the existing reviewed questions, requester identities and source times. Output: one spoken request per question, with the “Assistant,” cue. Codex preserves the question’s required facts.</li><li><strong>Speaker enrollment.</strong> Input: a short recording of the same person and its checked transcript. Output: the voice prompt for F5-TTS. Enrollment means giving TTS a voice example; it is not model training.</li><li><strong>Speech synthesis.</strong> Input: the spoken question and voice prompt. Output: candidate waveforms from the frozen F5-TTS v1 Base checkpoint and Vocos waveform decoder, using the existing fixed inference settings.</li><li><strong>Speech checks.</strong> Input: candidate waveforms and the intended question. Output: Parakeet transcripts and speaker-similarity scores. Check the whole question and wake word, then select among qualifying candidates. Three proper-name cases remain flagged for pronunciation review; their recordings are available but are not counted as word-accuracy passes. ECAPA is a speaker encoder; its cosine score measures embedding similarity and participates in selection, so it is not an independent human voice rating.</li><li><strong>Acoustic matching and insertion.</strong> Input: selected speech, the requester’s original recording level and a verified quiet gap in the preceding recording, when available. Output: level-matched speech with only missing background-noise power added, then a pause/question/resume clip. When no quiet gap can be verified, no background sound is added. No extra EQ or reverberation is applied. The new clips retain 18 seconds before the question and five seconds after it; the original PCM samples are copied exactly.</li><li><strong>Final verification.</strong> Input: the processed question waveform. Output: a second Parakeet check, an independent Whisper transcript and final speaker diagnostics. These are automatic checks; human naturalness and acoustic review remain open.</li></ol>'
 body+='<p><strong>Voice enrollment is separate from conversation history.</strong> '+str(enroll)+' new questions use conditioning speech recorded after the insertion time, as authorized for speakers with little earlier speech. Those clips and transcripts never enter the duplex model’s history or background preparation. Cards label these cases. Some comparison utterances also come from later speech and are for listening only. All 20 questions in the frozen six-meeting subset use earlier conditioning speech.</p><p>The recording clock stops during the synthetic question. The player clock continues. A listening excerpt is not evidence that a model can retain the full preceding meeting. Eight call insertions move slightly to an estimated word boundary; the original transcript cutoffs remain available in the data.</p><p><a href="../research/question-audio-complete/recipe.json">Frozen synthesis recipe</a> · <a href="../research/question-audio-complete/evaluation-subset.json">Frozen 20-question subset and fact checklists</a> · <a href="../research/question-audio-complete/library.json">Complete audio index</a> · <a href="question-plan.html">Four-stage project TODO</a></p></section>'
 body+='<section class="section" id="checks"><h2>What the automatic checks show</h2>'+p('For the 92 new processed question clips, Parakeet recognizes Assistant as the first word in '+str(sum(c['processed_asr']['cue_first'] for c in new))+'/92. Its full transcript matches the intended question after case, punctuation, number and contraction normalization in '+str(sum(c['processed_asr']['normalized_wer']==0 for c in new))+'/92. Allowing separately recorded acronym, compound and homophone spelling differences gives '+str(sum(c.get('processed_orthographic_match',False) for c in new))+'/92. Remaining differences stay visible in the cards below; they are not silently counted as correct speech.')+'<p>Three names need pronunciation review: Cytiva, Nynke, and the Marios/Petr pair. A recognizer may spell unfamiliar names incorrectly, and TTS may also mispronounce them. These clips are available for review and are not word-accuracy passes. Independent human judgments are still needed for naturalness and voice/acoustic similarity.</p></section>'
 body+='<section class="section" id="listen"><h2>Browse and listen</h2><div class="catalog-filters"><label>Source<select id="audio-source"><option value="all">All sources</option><option>AMI</option><option>Earnings calls</option></select></label><label>Meeting<select id="audio-meeting"><option value="all">All meetings</option>'+''.join('<option>'+e(m)+'</option>' for m in sorted({c['meeting'] for c in clips}))+'</select></label><label>Subset<select id="audio-subset"><option value="all">All questions</option><option value="frozen">Frozen 20-question subset</option><option value="enrollment">Later voice enrollment</option></select></label></div><p id="audio-count" aria-live="polite">105 questions shown</p>'
 for c in clips:
  base=c['base'];later=c['separate_enrollment_after_question'];f=c['catalog_id'] in frozen
  body+='<article class="catalog-question listen-card" id="'+c['slug']+'" data-source="'+e(c['dataset'])+'" data-meeting="'+c['meeting']+'" data-frozen="'+str(f).lower()+'" data-enrollment="'+str(later).lower()+'"><h3>'+e(c['meeting']+' · requester '+c['requester']+' · '+clock(c['source_time_seconds']))+'</h3><p class="question">'+e(c['question'])+'</p>'
  if 'requires' in c.get('selection_note',''):body+='<p><strong>Pronunciation review needed:</strong> '+e(c['selection_note'])+'</p>'
  score=c.get('speaker_check',{}).get('target_cosine',c.get('processed_speaker_check',{}).get('target_cosine'))
  if score is not None and score<.3:body+='<p><strong>Voice review priority:</strong> low similarity to the separate requester recording. This is a screening flag, not a verified identity error.</p>'
  if c['question']!=c['canonical_question']:body+='<p>This audio uses a retained alternative phrasing of the same question.</p>'
  body+='<p>'+('Frozen evaluation subset · ' if f else '')+e(c['study'])+(' · <strong>Later voice enrollment; TTS only</strong>' if later else ' · Earlier voice conditioning')+'</p><p><strong>Recording excerpt with inserted question</strong></p>'+player(base+c['public_injected'],'Inserted question '+c['catalog_id'])+'<p><button class="jump-question" data-start="'+str(c['synthetic_speech_playback_start_seconds'])+'">Play from the question</button></p><details><summary>Question alone, original voice and automatic checks</summary><p><strong>Synthetic question alone</strong></p>'+player(base+c['public_matched'],'Question alone '+c['catalog_id'])+'<p><strong>Original requester voice — listening reference only</strong></p>'+player(base+c['public_reference'],'Original voice '+c['voice'])
  if c.get('reference_text'):body+=p(c['reference_text'])
  if c.get('reference_start_seconds') is not None:body+=p('Comparison source interval: '+clock(c['reference_start_seconds'])+'–'+clock(c['reference_end_seconds'])+(' (after the question; excluded from model history).' if c.get('comparison_reference_after_question') else '.'))
  if score is not None:body+=p('ECAPA similarity to the separate requester recording: '+f'{score:.3f}'+'. The same proxy guided selection; human voice review is still required.')
  a=c.get('processed_asr',{});body+='<p><strong>Parakeet transcript:</strong> '+e(a.get('text','See the original study’s recorded checks.'))+'</p>'
  if c.get('whisper_text'):body+='<p><strong>Whisper transcript:</strong> '+e(c['whisper_text'])+'</p>'
  if a.get('normalized_wer',a.get('wer')) is not None:body+=p('Normalized word error rate: '+f"{100*a.get('normalized_wer',a.get('wer')):.1f}%"+'. Case, punctuation, common number forms and contractions are normalized. Compare the displayed transcripts for recognizer disagreements.')
  if c.get('conditioning_reference_start_seconds') is not None:body+=p('TTS conditioning interval: '+clock(c['conditioning_reference_start_seconds'])+'–'+clock(c['conditioning_reference_end_seconds'])+'.')
  body+=p('Source recording pauses at '+clock(c['source_time_seconds'])+'; synthetic speech occupies '+f"{c['synthetic_speech_playback_start_seconds']:.2f}–{c['synthetic_speech_playback_end_seconds']:.2f} seconds"+' in this player. Source speech before and after the insertion is unchanged.')
  if c.get('pause_adjustment_seconds'):body+=p('The insertion moves '+f"{c['pause_adjustment_seconds']:.2f} s"+' after the original transcript cutoff to avoid splitting a spoken word.')
  body+='</details></article>'
 body+='</section><footer class="section"><h2>Resources, source audio and limitations</h2><p>Each synthesis job uses one L40S 48 GB, with F5-TTS and Vocos sharing GPU 0. Two independent synthesis jobs can overlap; the maximum for this work is two GPUs. Source verification precedes synthesis. ASR and ECAPA checks follow sequentially on one L40S 48 GB, with Whisper added for final clips. Mixing and page generation use 0 GPUs. No model weights are trained and no S1/S2 system comparison is run here.</p><p>Original source audio: <a href="https://groups.inf.ed.ac.uk/ami/corpus/license.shtml">AMI Meeting Corpus, CC BY 4.0</a>, and <a href="https://github.com/revdotcom/speech-datasets/tree/main/earnings21">Earnings21, CC BY-SA 4.0</a>. The downloadable excerpts add synthetic speech and acoustic processing. The earnings-call PCM is decoded and resampled from the source MP3; AMI excerpts preserve source PCM. F5 weights use CC BY-NC 4.0. <a href="../research/question-audio-complete/provenance.json">Audio hashes and attribution</a>.</p><p>Automatic transcription and voice similarity help catch errors. They do not establish human naturalness, correct answers, long-history retention or duplex-system performance. The <a href="ami-question-audio.html">original three-model TTS comparison</a> and earlier audio pages remain available.</p></footer>'
 resources=json.loads((D/'resources.json').read_text())
 body=body.replace('</footer>','<p>Total allocation for this completion work: '+f"{resources['total_gpu_hours']:.6f} GPU hours"+', including the failed attempt and every retry/check. Measured maximum concurrency: two GPUs; none remain active.</p><details><summary>GPU count, role and allocation for each job</summary>'+table(1,'All audio-completion allocations. Every job uses one L40S 48 GB; a completed job does not establish speech quality.',['Job','Stage','State','GPU count / type / VRAM','GPU role','Allocation'],[[r['job'],{'source':'Source speech checks','tts':'Question synthesis','raw':'Candidate speech checks','post':'Final speech checks'}[r['stage']],r['state'],'1 × L40S 48 GB',e(r['gpu_role']),str(r['allocation_seconds'])+' s'] for r in resources['jobs']])+'</details></footer>')
 js="""for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('.jump-question'))b.onclick=()=>{const a=b.closest('article').querySelector('audio');a.currentTime=Number(b.dataset.start);a.play();};const filters=['audio-source','audio-meeting','audio-subset'].map(id=>document.getElementById(id));function update(){const [s,m,u]=filters.map(x=>x.value);let n=0;for(const c of document.querySelectorAll('.listen-card')){c.hidden=!((s==='all'||s===c.dataset.source)&&(m==='all'||m===c.dataset.meeting)&&(u==='all'||(u==='frozen'&&c.dataset.frozen==='true')||(u==='enrollment'&&c.dataset.enrollment==='true')));if(!c.hidden)n++;}document.getElementById('audio-count').textContent=n+' questions shown';}filters.forEach(x=>x.onchange=update);update();"""
 document('question-audio.html','Question audio library','ami-library',body,js)
 path=ROOT/'experiments/question-audio.html';html=path.read_text().replace('</style>','audio{width:100%;max-width:650px}button{font:inherit;padding:.5rem .8rem;max-width:100%;white-space:normal}details{margin:1rem 0}</style>');path.write_text(html);print('Rendered audio library:',len(clips),'questions')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
